acceptance_criteria: "Network, process and time budgets stop further probes; private output stays redacted; repeat runs retain command identity and scope. Typed SDK and CLI; compact TOON and JSON; typed refusals and remedies; README and example; read-only public tracker validation outside Git; focused local checks and full npm plus Bun CI gates."
resolution: "Reviewed read-only plans enforce process/network/deadline budgets, redact private output and preserve command identity and scope through compact no-git SDK/CLI receipts."
expected_result: "Network, process and time budgets stop further probes; private output stays redacted; repeat runs retain command identity and scope. Typed SDK and CLI; compact TOON and JSON; typed refusals and remedies; README and example; read-only public tracker validation outside Git; focused local checks and full npm plus Bun CI gates."
actual_result: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/194, merged 2026-10-23T17:41:41Z, merge e549225a60bc4f8fc264aa8f6cba42303da6a8a5: Reviewed read-only plans enforce process/network/deadline budgets, redact private output and preserve command identity and scope through compact no-git SDK/CLI receipts."
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T16:45:44.707Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against pinned core SDK plan and sibling README contracts: core plan owns durable steps and approval; ops scan/report gather findings; pm-swarm plans execution waves; pm-rlm owns model budgets. This feature only orchestrates a closed catalog of read-only diagnostic probes selected from observed failure codes. Plans bind command identity, tracker scope and resource ceilings; execution requires the reviewed plan digest. No scheduler, release template, arbitrary commands or tracker mutations. Reuse core settings, schema, canonical item readers and history verification; no dependency bump."
  "2026-10-23T16:54:08.583Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses a closed four-command read-only catalog: SDK schema, source item reads, per-item history verification, and a fixed registry HEAD. Directory scope and exact budgets are bound to the review digest. Every process reserves cost before dispatch; any exhausted ceiling stops later probes. Worker heap/output/deadline are capped, environment injection is removed, and receipts project only numeric counts plus fixed codes/remedies. Source reads avoid SDK cache and hook side effects. Initial focused checks verify non-git byte preservation and deterministic repeats."
  "2026-10-23T16:59:01.395Z",codex-agent,"The saturated host demonstrated actual shared-deadline enforcement on the public 149-item tracker: later probes stopped at the 60000 ms ceiling. Repeat validation now checks the required command identity and scope rather than requiring identical outcomes under different load. The linked-test wrapper default of 120 seconds expired during installed CLI startup; it is raised to 900 seconds while product budget ceilings remain unchanged. No runtime or cache files are committed."
  "2026-10-23T17:02:38.300Z",codex-agent,"Pinned SDK guarded linked-test metadata editing refused because the package peer baseline still permits hosts without item format 2. Existing history was preserved. Replaced the test link through normal remove/add operations with an explicit 900-second harness timeout, without changing package dependency pins. Public-scope source readers now defer folder traversal normalization and history item-id validation to core SDK contracts rather than duplicating them."
  "2026-10-23T17:04:44.943Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof completed: disabling only the process-ceiling guard made the resource regression fail (4 launches observed versus 0 allowed). Exact source bytes were restored. The standalone real-data validator is an acceptance harness under test, and the SDK usage example is Markdown documentation; neither adds unmeasured production runtime code. Focused module coverage before the final compatibility additions measured 100 percent statements, functions and lines; remaining branch cases are addressed by compiled CLI and JSON-Markdown reads."
  "2026-10-23T17:09:25.179Z",codex-agent,"SDK source inspection found normal readSettings may create schema scaffold files and silently return fallback defaults. The diagnostic now uses runWithConfigurationOnlySettings plus readSettingsWithMetadata for validated base settings, copies only scoped regular schema files into parent-owned disposable settings directories, and hydrates through core there. Parent cleanup also runs after worker timeout; settings/schema warnings fail closed. Added malformed settings, missing schema, file-backed custom types, traversal and schema-link regressions. Public validation before this hardening read 149 items across 306 unchanged files; final measurements will be refreshed."
  "2026-10-23T17:15:36.891Z",codex-agent,"Public non-git acceptance on the final settings-isolation implementation: 306 copied tracker files stayed byte-identical; 149 items, 11 schema types and 1927 item-history entries verified. First run completed in 46818 ms with 3 launches and 0 network requests; repeat retained exact plan/scope identities and stopped history at the shared deadline (60320 ms including termination/cleanup). One-process plan launched once and skipped two later probes. Full successful JSON receipt measured 448 bytes. Ready PR 194 opened; npm and Bun full-gate evidence will come from CI at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-23T17:17:21.274Z",codex-agent,"Final maintainability pass shares one tracker fingerprint helper with the existing expiry regressions and the standalone acceptance harness, avoiding copied test infrastructure under the unchanged zero-duplication policy. Dedicated settings/schema regression now passes with malformed empty settings correctly refused by the pinned SDK. README clarifies measured deadline termination/cleanup overhead. CI release matrix is running for PR 194."
  "2026-10-23T17:18:39.695Z",codex-agent,"Linked focused command now passes 19/19, with no failures or skips. The dedicated malformed-settings and optional-schema regression also passes independently. Initial full-matrix CI exposed duplication on the earlier pushed head; shared fingerprint and replay-identity helpers remove the repeated infrastructure while keeping the zero-duplication threshold unchanged. Final-head CI will be used for npm and Bun release-gate counts."
  "2026-10-23T17:28:43.922Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/39994176089 passed on commit 4a6f5a02340fb34a8db08755394b6ee2f8e75b05. Both Node 22 and Node 26 passed npm run release:check and bun run release:check: each gate reports 1422 tests, 1420 pass, 0 fail/cancel/TODO, and 2 pre-existing opt-in real-data skips. Coverage is 100/100/100/100 across all 34 measured source files; docstrings cover 283 declarations; duplication is 0 percent across 92 sources and 30228 lines. Both Windows packed npm/native Bun consumer jobs passed. A separate native Bun SDK smoke verified 11 schema types with one process and zero network requests. Local linked focused tests pass 19/19; typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings, duplication and changelog checks pass. No merge or release performed. Remaining limits: per-probe observations are not a concurrent snapshot, and deadline receipts can include termination/cleanup overhead. Core guarded test metadata editing remains unavailable with the package broad legacy peer baseline; normal remove/add preserved history and supplied the harness timeout."
